\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Peace, Doubting heart! my God's I am:
\par Who formed me man, forbids my fear;
\par The Lord hath called me by my name;
\par The lord protects, forever near;
\par His blood for me did once atone,
\par And still He loves and guards His own.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When, passing through the watery deep,
\par I ask in faith his promised aid,
\par The waves an awful distance keep,
\par And shrink from my devoted head;
\par Fearless their voilence I dare;
\par They cannot harm, for God is there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. To Him my heart of faith I turn,
\par And through the fire pursue my way;
\par The fire forgets its power to burn,
\par The lambent flames around me play;
\par I own His power, accept the sign,
\par And shout to prove the Saviour's mine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Sill nigh me, O my Savior, stand!
\par And guard in fierce temptation's hour;
\par Hide in the hollow of Thy hand,
\par Show forth in me Thy saving power,
\par Still be Thy arms my sure defence,
\par Nor earth nor hell shall pluck me thence.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. When darkness intercepts the skies
\par And sorrow's around me roll,
\par When high the storms of passion rise,
\par And half o'erwhelm my sinking soul;
\par My soul a suden calm shall feel,
\par And hear a whisper: Peace; be still.
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par    \f1 
